{"title":"2003 Pan African MO Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_Pan_African_MO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/f/01ff757258a4718f36865211f8d312e4a11ee031.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N_0=\\{0, 1, 2 \\cdots \\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"134\" height=\"18\" />. Find all functions: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/b/24b799ddb4a169e4facba0c49fda276c5109288b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N_0 \\to N_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"71\" height=\"15\" /> such that:\n</p><p>(1) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/b/42b11a391208e2c3e1209edfaa2eb29735a56c3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n) &lt; f(n+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"129\" height=\"20\" />, all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/f/bdfc6f3f9e88294dd799cabd2ec223e0fe2452c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\in N_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"53\" height=\"15\" />;\n</p><p>(2) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/e/64eb03e53983d05c3e97b121504a882e16901e22.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(2)=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" />;\n</p><p>(3) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/f/86f9146277644a2e2b34f2a629d1de97fdeb8836.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(mn)=f(m)f(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"151\" height=\"18\" />, all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/2/8e27242576a72bd7eeee032b1fd25499628e2522.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m, n \\in N_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"77\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_Pan_African_MO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/f/26f2422507f5401fbff1102154a111beb17146ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(mn) = f(m)f(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"151\" height=\"18\" />, we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/0/a3095ee2348cfc43c022549e572beb0426ee576d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(2) = f(2) \\cdot f(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"141\" height=\"20\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/d/b6dd0ff40babd7fbd0c3e3d3b019627c27949616.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1) = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" />.  Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/c/17c59bd9d20bcc9cd7fea79dd1f88c8d6332ce55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(0) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nBy trying smaller values, we suspect that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/e/78e4d0b2e6d053bfe0109e52affa87bcce39d9c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n) = n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" /> for all values in the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/4/ef46f7519c0f176611a9e4e7fe1b05012b2d0e35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"20\" height=\"15\" />.  To prove this, we would use <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Induction\" title=\"Induction\">induction</a> to show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/e/78e4d0b2e6d053bfe0109e52affa87bcce39d9c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n) = n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/6/1561519b61ec2fe81242bd03b74c66825d2ba12e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\le n \\le 2^k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"84\" height=\"18\" /> for all integer values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nThe base case works because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/4/6745b23d42ba61db8ff4816233e3067565bf64bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(0) = 0, f(1) = 1, f(2) = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"218\" height=\"18\" />.  For the inductive step, assume that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/e/78e4d0b2e6d053bfe0109e52affa87bcce39d9c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n) = n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/6/1561519b61ec2fe81242bd03b74c66825d2ba12e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\le n \\le 2^k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"84\" height=\"18\" /> for an integer value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />.  To prove this case, we need to prove that all values from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/2/eb28a5061e4e516fdcd8c183647fec0ca1bd613d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^k + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"17\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/3/473b67382183fc823e117858fef19aaf2ec23948.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{k+1}$\" width=\"32\" height=\"15\" /> also work.\n</p><p><br />\nNote that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/d/0dd017f11473756a14b11d36f076c66c091e1ba2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(2n) = f(2) \\cdot f(n) = 2 f(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"220\" height=\"18\" />.  Therefore, we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/9/f79e882e720cf6b1c084c2ac16045a09739c4892.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(2^{k+1}) = 2 \\cdot f(2^k) = 2^{k+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"204\" height=\"20\" />.  Additionally, given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> is an integer that satisfies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/5/63518d4bba918562df0dc86ba1869796b5695126.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{k+1} - 2m - 2 \\ge 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"145\" height=\"18\" />, we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/8/d3828dc327846b2f25838f72cf2856e7d8038b46.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(2^{k+1} - 2m) = 2 \\cdot f(2^k - m)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"231\" height=\"20\" />.  Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/2/1d26cc2caf222d731677077c51d5d929c2ff40d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^k - m$\" width=\"55\" height=\"15\" /> is within the range of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/6/1561519b61ec2fe81242bd03b74c66825d2ba12e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\le n \\le 2^k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"84\" height=\"18\" />, we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/f/c7fa80a26c0957eb8bb2b964c163de0e7eb137a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\cdot f(2^k - m) = 2^{k+1} - 2m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"207\" height=\"20\" />.  Furthermore, we must also have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/1/5e1301ab7585fcf3bbb7de7206e85116dd72e913.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(2^{k+1} - 2m - 2) = 2 \\cdot f(2^k - m - 1) = 2^{k+1} - 2m - 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"432\" height=\"20\" />.  Thus, we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/2/722fab455fe76789a608126cfa3a5c671a3390c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(2^{k+1} - 2m - 1) = 2^{k+1} - 2m - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"273\" height=\"20\" />.  Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> can be any integer that satisfies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/5/63518d4bba918562df0dc86ba1869796b5695126.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{k+1} - 2m - 2 \\ge 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"145\" height=\"18\" />, the value <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/d/7bda99d24a45f68330a3f60a60b24baefd971b42.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{k+1} - 2m - 2$\" width=\"112\" height=\"15\" /> can be any even integer.  Thus all numbers from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/3/473b67382183fc823e117858fef19aaf2ec23948.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{k+1}$\" width=\"32\" height=\"15\" /> are represented in the proof, so the inductive step holds.\n</p><p><br />\nTherefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/e/78e4d0b2e6d053bfe0109e52affa87bcce39d9c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n) = n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/6/1561519b61ec2fe81242bd03b74c66825d2ba12e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\le n \\le 2^k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"84\" height=\"18\" /> for any integer value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, so the only function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/b/24b799ddb4a169e4facba0c49fda276c5109288b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N_0 \\to N_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"71\" height=\"15\" /> that satisfies the three conditions is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/f/90ffa23149146f9d339ea4b3de21e9fe6d122f5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{f(n) = n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"82\" height=\"29\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_Pan_African_MO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_Pan_African_MO\" title=\"2003 Pan African MO\">2003 Pan African MO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_Pan_African_MO_Problems\" title=\"2003 Pan African MO Problems\">Problems</a></b>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b>First Problem</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_Pan_African_MO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2003 Pan African MO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_Pan_African_MO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2003 Pan African MO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_Pan_African_MO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2003 Pan African MO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_Pan_African_MO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2003 Pan African MO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_Pan_African_MO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2003 Pan African MO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_Pan_African_MO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2003 Pan African MO Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pan_African_MO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"Pan African MO Problems and Solutions\"> All Pan African MO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017202614\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.024 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.040 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 243/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 923/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 51/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7672/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.586      1 Template:Pan_African_MO_box\n100.00%    6.586      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:17998:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017202614 and revision id 114711. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}